RISC OS: particle smoke/clouds and the ground texture off by default.

The defaults for a new configuration only; flight.cfg keeps what the user
chose. Both are in the configuration dialog ("Draw Burning Smoke by
Particles", which also draws the clouds as particles, and "Use Ground
Texture"). Measured on riscos-mesa's renderer at 640x480, F-18 at Misawa
runway / at 10000 ft: 603M / 527M instructions a frame with the upstream
defaults, 358M / 192M without particles, 228M / 147M also without the
ground texture.

For YSCE 231e711. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-ysflight.

diff --git a/src/config/fsconfig.cpp b/src/config/fsconfig.cpp
index efdc62e..ba3aa67 100644
--- a/src/config/fsconfig.cpp
+++ b/src/config/fsconfig.cpp
@@ -91,6 +91,16 @@ void FsFlightConfig::SetDefault(void)
 
 	aircraftReliability=95;
 	aircraftTroubleFrequency=0.1;
+
+#ifdef __riscos__
+	// RISC OS draws with software OpenGL. Measured on riscos-mesa's
+	// renderer at 640x480 (instructions per frame, F-18 at Misawa / in the
+	// air): particle clouds and smoke are 40% / 64% of the frame, the
+	// ground texture 33% / 21% of what is left. Both can be turned back on
+	// in the configuration dialog.
+	useParticle=YSFALSE;
+	useOpenGlGroundTexture=YSFALSE;
+#endif
 }
 
 void FsFlightConfig::SetDetailedMode(void)
